From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Gino D." <25200363+zinosaure@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 20:25:36 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] tests: --compile-only compiles and validates every named
 compute case without the GPU

A change of the code Kyty generates is checked before any of it runs on the device. A failed case stops
the program; --compile-only <n> starts again at case n. With 0085 and 0086 alike, 265 of the 266 cases
pass; VectorAddcWritesPerLaneCarryOut fails its typed IR count in both.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
